    "title": "Resident calls 911 while burglars ransack Beverlywood home - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By City News Service ,\n9 hours ago\nPolice on Wednesday were investigating a break-in and burglary of a home in the Beverlywood section of West Los Angeles where someone inside called 911 while the residence was being ransacked.\nWant to get caught up on what's happening in SoCal every weekday afternoon? Click to follow The L.A. Local wherever you get podcasts.\nOfficers were sent to the home in the 9300 block of Bolton Road around 11:30 p.m. Tuesday, where two suspects entered the home by smashing a glass door before taking unspecified property, according to the Los Angeles Police Department.\nAt least two suspects entered the home while another waited in a getaway car described only as a black sedan last seen heading east, an officer said, citing preliminary findings.\nHe said the case was being investigated as \"a burglary/hot prowl.\"\nThe 911 call was made by a woman hiding in a bathroom at the home, according to media reports that indicated another home on the same block was burglarized over the weekend.\nFollow KNX News 97.1 FM\nTwitter | Facebook | Instagram | TikTok",
